  "result": "The six-question quiz on O4 is ready as `quizzes/0002.json`, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. I answered each item from its stem alone and found one defensible answer for each.\n\n- **Format:** There are four multiple-choice items and two one-word short items. The short items ask \"workflow or agent?\", so they have a single reply that can be matched.\n- **Coverage:** The quiz covers three things.\n  - **Control flow:** who owns it, and how to classify the makerspace assistant's designs.\n  - **Cost:** why a fixed workflow keeps cost per request predictable.\n  - **Deciding:** when a fixed workflow is the better choice, using the booking steps as the example.\n- **Stretch item:** Question 6 asks whether a fixed sequence that includes one model call is still a workflow.\n- **Ahead of the lessons:** There is no lesson on workflows versus agents yet, so this checks the objective itself and is ahead of your lessons. Unlike quiz 0001, I wrote it from my own knowledge and did not search for or cite a source.\n- **Misconception ids:** None of the multiple-choice options are tagged with a misconception id, because the workspace has no ids for this topic yet.\n\nDo you want a short lesson on workflows versus agents before you take the quiz?",
